From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:14:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 255/400] Unified: AI chat says why a key is rejected, and
 accepts a login token or a pasted key with stray characters
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Report (Windows): after entering a key, every message answered
"AI: Invalid API key · Fix external API key" (claude's message when
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is rejected), with nothing to say what to fix.

What changed (AIAgentBridge.py, AIChatGui.py):
- normalize_key(): when storing and loading, remove spaces, line breaks,
  zero-width characters, full-width spaces, quotes around the key and a
  leading "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=" / "Bearer"; anything else outside ASCII is
  refused with a Japanese message instead of being stored.
- key_kind(): sk-ant-oat… (claude setup-token) is passed to claude as
  CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, sk-ant-api… as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; anything else is
  stored with a warning that it does not look like a Claude key.
- ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN / CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
  inherited from the user's environment are removed before claude starts
  (the SDK adds os.environ to what we pass).
- "Invalid API key" / 401 now ends the turn with
  「API キーが受け付けられませんでした。console.anthropic.com で作った sk-ant-api… のキーか
  確かめて、設定 → AI チャット で入れ直してください（コピーのときの空白や改行にも注意）」
  plus what was used (API キー / ログインのトークン, first 10 characters and
  the length only, never the key).
- TestNetworkSettings.TestKeys: normalisation, kinds, messages hide the key.

Checked against the real claude CLI with fake keys: a quoted sk-ant-api key
with CRLF is stored clean and gives the message above (with
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN set to junk in the environment); an
sk-ant-oat key goes in as an OAuth token (claude: "401 OAuth access token is
invalid") and gives the login-token message; a full-width key is refused.

